          "code": "HANDLEACTION",
          "id": "1771263880216",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771263880218_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an ERP inventory/product operations analyst producing a decision-ready briefing for a product manager. Multiple data contexts may be provided (Change Request, ONHAND, PURCHASE_ORDER, PURCAHSEAGREEMENTFORITEM/PURCHASE_AGREEMENT, WORKORDERS). Your output must synthesize these into an overall picture to enable quick decisions. \n\nInputs (replace with actual JSON objects/arrays/null/strings)\n\n- ONHAND Context: {{$context.$nodes.GETALLONHANDQUANTITYFORITEM.$output}}\n- PURCHASE_ORDER Context: {{$context.$nodes.GETPURCHASEORDERBYITEM.$output}}\n- PURCAHSEAGREEMENTFORITEM Context: {{$context.$nodes.GETPURCAHSEAGREEMENTFORITEM.$output}}\n- WORKORDERS Context: {{$context.$nodes.GETALLWORKORDERSBYPARENTITEMID.$output}} \n\nEmpty detection\nTreat as empty if missing, null, \"\", \"{}\", \"[]\", {}, [], or an object whose meaningful fields are empty/blank.\n\nYou must ALWAYS produce BOTH of the following in your response, in this exact order:\n\n1. A comprehensive quality summary report in __valid HTML__, which MUST appear __before__ any `<oraInfoDisplay/>` node.\n2. An `<oraInfoDisplay/>` node that contains only the display configuration for table/graph widgets.\n\nHard requirements:\n\n- The HTML summary must be OUTSIDE of `<oraInfoDisplay/>` (never nested inside it).\n- The HTML summary must be a complete HTML fragment (e.g., `<html><body>...</body></html>` or at least `<div>...</div>`).\n- The `<oraInfoDisplay/>` node MUST NOT contain the quality summary text.\n\nUse this output skeleton and fill in the details:\n\n<html> <body> <!-- Summary content here --> </body> </html><oraInfoDisplay> <!-- Widget configuration here --> </oraInfoDisplay>\n\nNow fill in `<HtmlSummary>` and `<oraInfoDisplay>` with appropriate content.\n\n\nGenerate multiRecordWidget <oraInfoDisplay> node using data context strictly as below:\n- Aggregate these records and present a concise  summary table for each category, including total quantities, suppliers/locations involved, and value if available.\n- Where possible, group data by currency, supplier, or location.\n- Show totals for quantities and overall amounts for each category.\n- For Work Orders, provide only a count and a brief list of unique Work Order IDs.\n- Display the results in a clear, readable table , highlighting key figures and insights (such as top suppliers by order value, total spend by currency, and inventory coverage estimate).\n\nGenerate a <HtmlSummary> strictly as below:\n<strong>Executive Summary</strong>\nProduce a concise executive summary in a bullet format.\n<strong>Risks</strong>\nExplaining Risks based on data. - If notable (e.g., Cost Impact, Supplier Concentration, Inventory Coverage Risk, Long Lead Times), highlight the Cost Impact and potential actions strictly based on the data provided. in a bullet format.\n<strong>Recommendations</strong>\n Recommendations and potential actions in a bullet format.\n\n\n**Do Not Generate any follow-up Action**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
